<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/3rd-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mercenary War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/241-bce">241</a>–<a href="/years/238-bce">238 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">Mercenary</a> War was a revolt by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>'s unpaid mercenary army and its Libyan subjects from 241 to 238 BCE, following the First Punic War. The rebellion threatened Carthage itself before it was crushed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamilcar-barca">Hamilcar Barca</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> used the crisis to seize <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a>, weakening the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punic-empire">Punic Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mercenary-war.jpg" alt="Mercenary War" width="320" height="156" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Libyan_Revolt,_shekel,_241-238_BC.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…enabling the rapid assembly of large and diverse forces but creating chronic weaknesses in loyalty and cohesion, as the <b>Mercenary War</b> of 241–238 BCE demonstrated, when unpaid veterans of the First Punic War turned on Carthage itself in a brutal conflict that Gustave Flaubert later fictionalised in Salammbô.</blockquote><a href="/empire/punic-empire">Punic Empire · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>In 238 BCE, after its defeat in the First Punic War, Carthage surrendered Sardinia to Rome during the <b>Mercenary War</b>, and with Corsica the island became the Roman province of Corsica et Sardinia.</blockquote><a href="/culture/nuragic-civilisation">Nuragic civilisation · Legacy</a></li><li><blockquote>It became an ally of Carthage and part of the Punic Empire but often kept its distance, joining the rebels in the <b>Mercenary War</b> of 240 to 238 BCE.</blockquote><a href="/state/utica">Utica</a></li></ul></section>
